Figure 11, depicting H&E-stained injection site sections two weeks post-immunization, illustrates that Nano-11 induces significantly less residual inflammation compared to aluminum hydroxide (AH) adjuvant. The left panel (AH) shows extensive granulomatous inflammation, characterized by dense aggregates of immune cells within the skeletal muscle. In contrast, the right panel (Nano-11) reveals a much milder inflammatory response with relatively few macrophages arranged in slender cords within the connective tissue, indicating a more transient and resolved local reaction.